.TH REBELSOFGAMING 1 "2026-10-31" "Rebels of Gaming" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rebelsofgaming \- native app of the Rebels of Gaming clan platform
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rebelsofgaming
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIrog://LINK\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rebelsofgaming
is the native Linux client of the Rebels of Gaming clan platform: news, forum, wiki, direct messages,
squads, members, calendar, matches, game servers, gallery, downloads, uploads and \- with the right
permissions \- server control, moderation and administration.
.PP
Sign-in happens in the system browser. The device token is stored in the Secret Service keyring
(GNOME Keyring, KWallet, KeePassXC); without a keyring it is kept in memory only.
.PP
If the app is already running, a second start hands its arguments (for example a
.B rog://
link) to the running instance and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-x11
Use X11 (or XWayland) even in a Wayland session.
.TP
.B \-\-wayland
Use native Wayland.
.TP
.B \-\-gamemode
Start in game mode (full screen, larger controls), as in Steam Deck gaming mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-environment= NAME
Select the platform environment
.RB ( production ,
.BR staging ,
.BR local );
for development only.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ROG_DISPLAY
.B x11
or
.BR wayland ,
same as the options above.
.TP
.B ROG_GAMEMODE
.B 1
starts in game mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rebelsofgaming/
Settings (settings.json, linux.json).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/rebelsofgaming/
Encrypted offline copies of wiki pages.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://rebelsofgaming.com/ \- https://github.com/Rebels-of-Gaming/rebelsofgaming-linux
